# Reply — the `>= 85` count pin fights baseline regeneration (IMPORTANT)

Fixed in the same commit as the baseline regeneration (`17cf21dc`). The magic number is gone; the test now asserts only non-drifting invariants:

- `files.length > 0` — the baseline pins the current debt set;
- `files.length <= 85` — never exceeds the gh-1251 historical maximum;
- every entry is a production `.js/.mjs/.cjs` file that exists in the repo;
- every entry is a `{ pct, lines }` object with `pct > 1` and `lines` a positive integer (pins the v2 absolute-lines shape).

Future dedup landings (gh-1245…gh-1250) now only require regenerating `duplication-baseline.json` — this test will keep passing as long as the debt set keeps shrinking within the historical bound.

